{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be part of your care team. You came in last night after taking some tramadol and Phenergan. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I took more than I should have. I was arguing with my mom, and I just couldn’t handle it. I wanted it to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re going through that. It takes a lot of courage to come in. Were you planning to hurt yourself?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I didn’t want to live anymore. I’ve been so overwhelmed—my pain, my mom needing me, everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:19:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for being honest. We’re going to keep you safe here. You had a brief episode of low oxygen and were given Narcan. You responded well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:20:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember waking up in the ER, confused. I didn’t think I’d need that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tramadol in high doses can suppress breathing. We’re monitoring you closely. No signs of serotonin syndrome or heart issues, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on tramadol for my endometriosis pain. It’s the only thing that helps sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But because of the overdose, we’re stopping tramadol for now. Psychiatry is adjusting your other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:24:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain? It’s been really bad lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll manage it with the lidocaine patch and other non-opioid options. Your gynecology team can help long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:26:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I guess I just feel stuck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re not alone. We’re here to support you. A CT scan of your head was normal—no bleeding or stroke. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:28:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried about brain damage or something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. Your labs are improving—kidney function, electrolytes, all looking stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:30:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had liver issues before from past drug use, but I’ve been clean since pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your liver enzymes are normal now. That’s great. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. Still sad, but not as foggy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. Your vitals are stable. Psychiatry lowered your Seroquel to 150mg at night and added a PRN dose for anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:03:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on 300mg. Will that make me more anxious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re adjusting it carefully. The lower dose may help with side effects, and you can take the PRN if you feel overwhelmed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I just don’t want to spiral again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re preventing that. You’re medically stable, and you’ll be transferred to inpatient psychiatry for ECT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:07:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "ECT again? It helped before, but I’m scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a strong option for treatment-resistant depression. The team will go over the risks and benefits with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember memory fog afterward, but I felt better for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The goal is to help you regain stability. You’ll be medically cleared for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:11:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my thyroid and acid reflux? I’m on levothyroxine and ranitidine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep both. Your thyroid levels are stable, and ranitidine helps with stomach irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:13:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want other things flaring up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day. Your labs are excellent—better than admission. You’re cleared for transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous but ready, I think."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. You’ll go to extended psychiatric care. They’ll start ECT soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:33:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need to stop eating tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, nothing after midnight the night before your first ECT. The team will confirm the schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds? What do I take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue levothyroxine, ranitidine, prenatal vitamins, lidocaine patch, and the Depo shot. Seroquel is now 150mg at night, plus PRN."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:37:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No tramadol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. It’s too risky given your history. We’ll work with pain management later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:39:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I want to get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will. You’ve already taken the hardest step—asking for help. We’re all rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:41:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. For listening, I mean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care. The transport team will be here soon to take you to psychiatry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll miss my baby. I hope I can get back to her soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:44:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Focus on healing now. The stronger you get, the sooner you’ll be back with her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what I’m fighting for."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:46:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Then keep going. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:48:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all anyone can ask. Take it one step at a time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-06-18 09:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-06-20 18:25:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman was admitted after a suicide attempt involving intentional overdose of tramadol and Phenergan, following an argument with her mother whom she cares for. She has a history of refractory bipolar disorder and depression with prior suicide attempts and ECT, opioid use disorder (now sober since pregnancy), endometriosis with chronic pain, hypothyroidism, and GERD. In the ED, she had transient hypoxia and reduced responsiveness, responded to Narcan, and was medically stabilized. She was monitored for 48 hours without complications, with normal CT head and improving labs. Tramadol was discontinued, Seroquel was reduced to 150mg nightly with PRN dosing for agitation, and she was medically cleared for transfer to inpatient psychiatry for ECT. She was discharged to extended psychiatric care with stable vital signs and clear mental status.",
    "problems": [
      "Poisoning by other synthetic narcotics, intentional self-harm, initial encounter",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Poisoning by other antiepileptic and sedative-hypnotic drugs, intentional self-harm, initial encounter",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Opioid abuse, uncomplicated",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Endometriosis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
